{
  "about": "Feature-level case catalogue (extrude, revolve, fillet, chamfer, shell) for differential testing; companion to cases.json. Units: mm and degrees. Every kernel builds exactly these inputs: cad-geom (crates/cad-geom/src/sweep.rs and later features), and ASM via a Fusion design (sketch + feature API, probe v6). A profile lies in 'plane' (origin, unit x, unit y; normal z = x × y) and is a list of closed loops in plane coordinates; loop orientation in the file is arbitrary (the loop enclosing the others is the outer boundary). Segments: {line: {a, b}}, {arc: {c, r, a0, sweep}} (start angle a0 from plane x towards plane y, signed sweep, + = counter-clockwise about the normal), {circle: {c, r}} (a whole loop). Extrude: the region swept along the plane normal from offset 'from' to 'to' (either order). Revolve: the region rotated about the world 'axis' line by 'angle' (right-hand rule about axis.dir, starting in the profile plane); the axis lies in the plane and does not cross the region's interior. Fillet / chamfer / shell act on the body of case 'base'; 'edges' and 'faces' are given by a point (world mm) lying on the entity.",
